	(text "BQ24074: OVP 10.5 V, OUT regulated to 4.4 V, charges to 4.2 V, TI SLUS810N.\nR21 ISET 1.78k: ICHG = 890 / 1780 = 500 mA, 0.5C for the assumed 1000 mAh cell.\nR23 ILIM 1.58k: about 1 A if EN2=1, EN1=0, which this strapping never selects. EN2 is tied low, so only USB100 and USB500 are reachable.\nLeaving ILIM open disables charging, per the datasheet, so R23 stays fitted.\nEN1 reset default is low (GPIO and 285k internal pull-down): 100 mA. Firmware sets 500 mA.\nCHG_CE_N high disables charging. R24 keeps it low until firmware runs.\nTMR and ITERM left open deliberately: datasheet defaults (default timers, 10% termination).\nTS has a fixed 10k because the assumed battery has no thermistor, per the datasheet. Battery must be protected.\nR20 and R25 remove the charger from the circuit. R26 (DNP) keeps battery power if the charger is removed:\nfit R26 ONLY with U4 removed. Never fit it with U4 in place.\nMECHANICAL: JST-PH LiPo polarity varies between vendors. Confirm against the real cell."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "464fe4d6-821e-5b1e-84e9-4b523e91518d")
	)
)
